        "media": [
          {
            "duration": 12.833,
            "height": 1080,
            "thumbnail_url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2108663568958943233/img/NjygtLsNOHYmWBDY.jpg",
            "type": "video",
            "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2108663568958943233/vid/avc1/1080x1080/IZeDFlRpAcrn5d5T.mp4?tag=29",
            "width": 1080
          }
        ],
        "name": "DogeDesigner",
        "text": "BREAKING: Venezuela’s telecom regulator, Conatel, has officially authorized Starlink to provide satellite internet nationwide. 🇻🇪\n\nAfter June’s earthquakes damaged phone and internet networks, Starlink provided more than 1,600 kits to support rescue teams, medical staff and humanitarian groups.\n\nNow, this approval opens the door to connecting more communities, giving people more choice and new opportunities to learn, work and stay connected.",
        "url": "https://x.com/cb_doge/status/2108663596569989321",
        "verified": true,
        "verified_type": "individual"
      },
      "retweet": null,
